_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Avoid duplicated login logic**

The login steps are duplicated across multiple tests, which could lead to maintenance issues.

Consider creating a custom Cypress command for login to avoid duplication:

```javascript
// Add to cypress/support/commands.js
Cypress.Commands.add('loginAsAdmin', () => {
  cy.visit('/wp-admin');
  cy.get('#user_login').type('admin');
  cy.get('#user_pass').type('password');
  cy.get('#wp-submit').click();
  cy.get('body.wp-admin').should('exist');
});

// Then in your test file:
it('Can access network admin', () => {
  cy.loginAsAdmin();

  // Go to network admin
  cy.visit('/wp-admin/network/');
  cy.get('body.network-admin').should('exist');
});
```

