_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Do not render AJAX messages as HTML.**

Line 108 interpolates `message` straight into markup. If the AJAX handler ever returns unsanitised content, this becomes an admin-side XSS sink. Build the notice with DOM APIs and `.text()` instead.  


<details>
<summary>🔒 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 		showNotice: function (type, message) {
-			const $notice = $( '<div class="wpst-notice ' + type + '"><p>' + message + '</p></div>' );
+			const safeType = [ 'success', 'error', 'warning' ].includes( type ) ? type : 'warning';
+			const $notice  = $( '<div>' ).addClass( 'wpst-notice ' + safeType );
+
+			$( '<p>' ).text( message ).appendTo( $notice );

 			// Add notice to the page
-			$( '.wpst-notices' ).html( $notice );
+			$( '.wpst-notices' ).empty().append( $notice );
```
</details>

