![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

These new tests are a great addition for verifying the plugin's core functionality. To improve them further, you could refactor them to reduce duplication and improve maintainability by following some Cypress best practices.

*   **DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself):** The `cy.loginAsAdmin()` and `cy.visit('/wp-admin/plugins.php')` calls are repeated in each of the new tests. This setup logic can be moved into a `beforeEach` hook within a new `describe` block that groups these related tests. This makes the tests cleaner and faster.

*   **Use Constants for Selectors:** The plugin slug `wp-plugin-starter-template-for-ai-coding` is a long string used in multiple selectors. Defining it as a constant makes the tests easier to read and maintain, especially if the slug ever changes.

*   **Scoped Queries with `.within()`:** For assertions on elements within a larger component (like the plugin row or the modal), using `.within()` makes tests clearer, more robust, and less likely to break from unrelated UI changes.

Here is an example of how you could refactor these tests:

```javascript
    const PLUGIN_SLUG = 'wp-plugin-starter-template-for-ai-coding';
    const PLUGIN_ROW_SELECTOR = `tr[data-slug="${PLUGIN_SLUG}"]`;

    describe('Plugin functionality on the plugins page', () => {
        beforeEach(() => {
            cy.loginAsAdmin();
            cy.visit('/wp-admin/plugins.php');
        });

        it('Plugin row is visible and has the correct name', () => {
            cy.get(PLUGIN_ROW_SELECTOR).should('be.visible').within(() => {
                cy.get('.plugin-title strong').should('contain', 'WordPress Plugin Starter Template');
            });
        });

        it('Update source selector link is present in the plugin row', () => {
            cy.get(PLUGIN_ROW_SELECTOR)
                .find('.wpst-update-source-selector')
                .should('exist');
        });

        it('Update source modal opens and displays source options', () => {
            cy.get(PLUGIN_ROW_SELECTOR).find('.wpst-update-source-selector').click();

            cy.get('#wpst-update-source-modal').should('be.visible').within(() => {
                cy.get('input[value="wordpress.org"]').should('exist');
                cy.get('input[value="github"]').should('exist');
                cy.get('input[value="gitea"]').should('exist');
                cy.get('#wpst-save-source').should('exist');
            });
        });

        it('Update source modal can be closed', () => {
            cy.get(PLUGIN_ROW_SELECTOR).find('.wpst-update-source-selector').click();
            cy.get('#wpst-update-source-modal').should('be.visible');

            cy.get('#wpst-update-source-modal .wpst-modal-close').click();
            cy.get('#wpst-update-source-modal').should('not.be.visible');
        });
    });
```

